            <div xml:id="d471">

                <pb facs="0639" n="545" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg545"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.6363 Standard Oil/362: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Persia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kornfeld</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-05-03T10:00:00+03:25"><hi rendition="#italic">May 3, 1924—10
                                a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 3—5:30 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>36. Bill to ratify Sinclair contract was introduced in Mejliss by Prime Minister
                    on April 19th. I have learned from reliable source <pb facs="0640" n="546"
                        xml:id="pg546"/> that a protest renewing the Khoshtaria claims has been
                    addressed to the Persian Government by the British.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kornfeld</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
